.Dd July 7, 2026
.Dt JC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jc
.Nd provision a jj repository and its workspaces from a config file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads a UCL-formatted configuration file and provisions a local
dev workspace managed by
.Xr jj 1 .
It initializes a colocated jj repository, registers the configured git
remotes, fetches from them, and creates one jj workspace per
configured workspace.
.Pp
.Nm
is run in the dev workspace: the directory that holds
.Pa jc.conf .
Each configured workspace is created as a subdirectory of it named
.Ar name Ns .jj .
The workspace named
.Dq default
is jj's initial workspace and holds the repository store; each
additional workspace is a linked jj workspace sharing that repository.
The default workspace is colocated with git, so standard git tools
work directly in it; linked workspaces are managed by jj alone.
.Pp
.Nm
is idempotent.
Running it again against an already-provisioned dev workspace
reconciles it with the config: missing remotes and workspaces are
added and fetched, and existing ones are left untouched.
It never discards local work.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is UCL.
It recognizes the following top-level keys.
.Bl -tag -width workspaces
.It Cm remotes
An array of git remotes to register on the repository.
Each element is an object with the keys:
.Bl -tag -width name
.It Cm name
The local name of the remote.
.It Cm src
The git URL fetched from.
.El
.It Cm workspaces
An array of workspaces to create.
One workspace must be named
.Dq default .
Each element is an object with the keys:
.Bl -tag -width name
.It Cm name
The jj workspace name.
The workspace is created in the subdirectory
.Ar name Ns .jj .
.El
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width jc.conf
.It Pa jc.conf
Configuration file, read from the current directory.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Given
.Pa jc.conf :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
remotes = [
  {name: "upstream", src: "https://github.com/allanjude/uclcmd.git"}
]

workspaces = [
  {name: "default"},
  {name: "man-page"}
]
.Ed
.Pp
running
.Nm
in the directory holding it produces:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\&./default.jj/     colocated jj repository and initial workspace
\&./man-page.jj/    linked jj workspace
.Ed
.Pp
with the
.Va upstream
remote registered and fetched.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jj 1
